{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-017",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 17,
  "title": "Job 17",
  "display_title": "Job 17",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 17,
  "sortOrder": 18017,
  "verseCount": 16,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:17:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "My breath is corrupt, my days are extinct, the graves are ready for me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 17:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:17:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:17:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Are there not mockers with me? and doth not mine eye continue in their provocation?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 17:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:17:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:17:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Lay down now, put me in a surety with thee; who is he that will strike hands with me?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 17:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:17:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:17:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "For thou hast hid their heart from understanding: therefore shalt thou not exalt them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 17:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:17:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:17:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "He that speaketh flattery to his friends, even the eyes of his children shall fail.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 17:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:17:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:17:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "He hath made me also a byword of the people; and aforetime I was as a tabret.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 17:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:17:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:17:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Mine eye also is dim by reason of sorrow, and all my members are as a shadow.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 17:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:17:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:17:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Upright men shall be astonied at this, and the innocent shall stir up himself against the hypocrite.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 17:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:17:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:17:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "The righteous also shall hold on his way, and he that hath clean hands shall be stronger and stronger.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 17:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:17:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:17:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "But as for you all, do ye return, and come now: for I cannot find one wise man among you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 17:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:17:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:17:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "My days are past, my purposes are broken off, even the thoughts of my heart.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 17:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:17:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:17:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "They change the night into day: the light is short because of darkness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 17:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:17:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:17:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "If I wait, the grave is mine house: I have made my bed in the darkness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 17:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:17:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:17:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "I have said to corruption, Thou art my father: to the worm, Thou art my mother, and my sister.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 17:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:17:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:17:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "And where is now my hope? as for my hope, who shall see it?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 17:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:17:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:17:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "They shall go down to the bars of the pit, when our rest together is in the dust.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 17:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:17:16"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
